  "Question": "A football game was played between two teams, the Cougars and the Panthers. The two teams scored a total of \\(34\\) points, and the Cougars won by a margin of \\(14\\) points. How many points did the Panthers score?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10\\)",
    "B": "\\(14\\)",
    "C": "\\(17\\)",
    "D": "\\(20\\)",
    "E": "\\(24\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "If we remove the Cougars' extra \\(14\\) points, their score becomes equal to the Panthers' score. The remaining total is therefore two copies of the Panthers' score:\n\\[\n34-14=20.\n\\]\nDividing equally gives \\(20\\div2=10\\) points for the Panthers, choice A.",
